  "_comment": "Companies whose ATS boards are scanned directly, on top of Adzuna/Reed/Indeed/hiring.cafe/LinkedIn. These give clean company names and full job descriptions (better sponsor matching), and they are a big part of the Netherlands and Ireland coverage, where the aggregator feeds are thinnest. The location filter in scan.py keeps only NL / Belgium / London / Ireland / Canada / remote-US roles, so a broad list is safe. 'ats' may be any board findform.BOARDS knows: greenhouse, ashby and lever have their own fetchers in scan.py; smartrecruiters, recruitee, workable, personio and teamtailor are read through findform.board_jobs(). The slug is in the careers URL. Run `python scan.py --verify` to test entries. Every slug below was verified live, and the NL/IE/BE block was chosen by counting how many roles each board actually had in those markets on the day it was added. Nov 2026: the home-domain employers (home-domain.json) whose public board could be found and checked were added at the end; the rest run Workday or their own careers stack, which this list cannot read, and still arrive through the aggregators.",
